Temporary workaround for native background Responses failing in OSS builds after
the upstream provider returns a queued or in-progress response.

https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/32782
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/32784
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/17204

The image intentionally excludes litellm_enterprise, so remove its background
managed-object persistence side effect while preserving native create, retrieve,
and cancel forwarding. Preserve the client-visible response ID across retrieval
and cancellation instead of re-encrypting it on every response. Remove this
patch when the pinned upstream release passes verify_background.py without it;
retain the regression check.

